    <title>
      <narrative xml:lang="en">Preservation and Interpretation of the Early 20th-Century Spooners Cotton Ginnery on Saint Kitts</narrative>
    </title>
    <description type="1">
      <narrative xml:lang="en">One of the first in the Caribbean to transition from sugar to cotton production at the turn of the 20th century, Spooners cotton ginnery is the only surviving ginnery of its kind on St. Kitts. This project, which includes conservation and community engagement for the long-term sustainable management of the site, directly supports the U.S. embassys efforts to promote economic development and youth employment through heritage tourism.</narrative>
    </description>
