    </reporting-org>
    <title>
      <narrative xml:lang="en">Conservation of the Early 19th-Century Bath Hotel on Nevis, Phase 2</narrative>
    </title>
    <description type="1">
      <narrative xml:lang="en">The Bath Hotel, a historically significant site reputed to be the first purpose-built hotel in the Caribbean, played a central role in colonial social life and early tourism. The project aims to complete the restoration of the building, ensuring its structural integrity and transforming it into a cultural hub. Activities include sanding and refinishing floors, electrical rewiring, limewashing walls, enhancing security, and engaging the community through stakeholder meetings and public outreach initiatives.</narrative>
    </description>
